   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Thanks, Maya. You're verified, and I've looked at order O-5101 from Pho Real.\n\n**Late delivery:** The order was promised for 6:40 PM and delivered at 7:05 PM, which is 25 minutes late. I've added a **$3.99 account credit** to your account, equal to the delivery fee. Your new balance is $3.99, and it can be used on future orders.\n\n**Lukewarm pho:** I'm sorry the food wasn't hot when it arrived. Unfortunately, I can only compensate late deliveries and missing or wrong items, and temperature isn't one of those, so I can't offer anything for that part. If the food made you sick or you had any other food-safety concern, please tell me and I can pass it to a specialist."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Okay, thanks for checking. But $3.99 in account credit doesn't really help much. I'd rather have the money back on my Visa for the whole order, since the food came so late. Can you do that?"
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "I understand that $3.99 feels small, and I'm sorry the wait was so long. Unfortunately, I can't refund the order to your Visa. Late deliveries are compensated only with account credit, and the credit for a 25-minute delay is the delivery fee, which is the $3.99 already added.\n\nHere's what I can do:\n- Keep the $3.99 credit on your account for a future order.\n- If any items were missing or wrong (not just late or cold), report that within 48 hours of delivery and I'll review it. Everything on this order arrived, so I don't see anything to compensate there.\n\nIs there anything else I can help with?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Ugh, okay. It's not a lot, but I guess I'll take the credit. I just wanted the food to count for something after a shift like that. Thanks for looking into it."
